+Alternating RaD producers in the explicit reversed23/25 fixed basis
+
+Claim. The source/auxiliary/data geometry of PR40 composes with PR41's
+alternating23 and25 ORIGINAL-envelope producers after replacing each entire
+local contribution by its freshly certified fixed-I+J profile. With copied
+centers and all paid endpoints retained, the resulting exact certificate gives
+kappa=4099494519/10^14. This is a conditional asymptotic saving under the
+inherited physical/analytic interfaces, not a practical performance claim.
+
+Provenance. RaD/hipotures PR41 and checkpoint7e488e6b supply the changed pair
+ordering and addition associations. icekylinx PR32/36 supplies fixed-profile
+and copied-center methods; James Chang PR34 supplies reversed prescriptions;
+PR37/39/40 supplies the explicit source/corner integration and exhaustive
+both-fixed compatibility. Dominik Scholz, Zhihao Chen, Paureel, Swapnil Jain
+and preceding contributors retain their topology/analytic credits. This
+package contributes the source-bound composition and fresh exact controls;
+it does not claim the new producer family as its own discovery.
+
+1. Finite changed producer and physical schedule
+
+For each h=23,25 the abstract sources are precisely all lexicographic triples
+t_T, T in C([h],3), under H=I-J/9. PR41's alternating-reverse rule reverses
+the ORDER of complete global pairs for odd common points, leaving within-pair
+order and the tail intact. It changes only addition-DAG construction; its
+source enumeration and designated common-point exclusion/total outputs remain
+the same. The pinned point_order_search.py is required to reproduce this rule;
+the old public producer_search.py alone does not implement the wrapper.
+
+Fresh DAG/source audits reconstruct every integer support, disjoint addition,
+actual original common-core/cover, designated exclusion and total, and the
+complete scalar JLV=I identity. Original non-source cores have size1 or2.
+Every original envelope lies in a common-point hyperplane sum(x)=3x_i, where
+x^T H x=sum_(j!=i)x_j^2, hence is nondegenerate. Legal original carrier links
+preserve space inclusion and strict event order; slot allocation, output
+protection and terminal incidences are checked separately. Positive signed
+labels or their rank histograms do NOT replace these original envelopes.
+
+Exactlyh retained centers have frame U_i=ker(1^t-3e_i^t), one designated
+terminal use, and no later ordinary consumer. Each terminal has full rankh-1
+inside U_i. The literal original-matching schedule has R23=36685,R25=48479
+roles. These values differ from earlier generic/common-basis prose and are
+bound to the new source/receipt hashes.
+
+The reversible scalar word L,J,L^-1,V,L,J,L^-1,V injects
+JLz+JL(z+Vx)=JLVx=x and restores every arbitrary auxiliary vector z.
+This algebra holds for any correctly compiled reversible L with the checked
+source/sink maps; it does not extrapolate from a small finite test. Both
+complement orientations retain the same nested differences. Fresh full
+scalar/frame/schedule checks and complete dirty-source/auxiliary basis replays
+of38456 and50779 vectors at the actual dimensions support the implementation; inherited complete-stream/tape realization remains an
+explicit conditional interface.
+
+2. A single explicit common basis, unchanged by the new DAGs
+
+Fix a=23,b=25,m=575,d=47, I=(0,...,22), and the PR34/37 controlled permutation
+completion with first-d row labels R=[I,22,I] and last-d inverse-column labels
+C=[I,0,I]. Use the SAME common rational basis
+ K=T_M((I23+J23) tensor(I25+J25))
+for every role and transition. There is no generic factor, runtime basis
+adapter, gather or uncharged permutation.
+
+The source triple projector becomes p xi, with
+ p=t+3*1, xi=(t-10/[3(h+1)]*1)^t/2.
+All coordinates are nonzero for every1771+2300 actual source triple. Their
+coordinate products are31/18 inside and-5/24 outside at h23, and68/39 inside
+and-5/26 outside at h25. Addition associations do not alter this line family.
+The PR40 saved exhaustive certificate covers its entire Cartesian product of
+4073300 pairs:191445100 nonzero prefixes and1409361800 ordered-zero regressions.
+Its universal zero proof comes from inherited exact rank-cut identities;
+nonvanishing comes from admissible-prime complete-prefix replays, with every
+failed primary pair preserved and successfully replayed. The default portable
+compatibility check rechecks source pins, coverage and rational fallback
+controls; it does not misreport that as a new exhaustive run.
+
+Consequently all data corners, both boundary restriction trees, nullity47,
+and the contiguous physical blocks remain identical to PR40:
+9 singletons,21,17,481. The21 block uses rows1..21/columns553..573; the17
+block rows28..44/columns530..546; middle481 rows/cols47..527. Each actual
+triple pair occurs once in each data bank, giving2N such data corners.
+
+3. Why arbitrary NEW local matrices transfer
+
+Actual controlled permutations give for ANY local A and B:
+ first23/last23 corner of A tensor(v nu): diag(v_i) A diag(nu_(j+2));
+ first25/last25 corner of(p xi)tensor B: diag(p_r) B diag(xi_c),
+where r=(0,...,22,22,0),c=(22,0,0,...,22).
+These are literal index identities checked by the inherited geometry, not
+rank-only assertions. All diagonal factors are nonzero for every source.
+Thus the actual ordered profile of ANY fresh fixed local matrix transfers
+unchanged; no additional generic nonvanishing condition on either local basis
+is required. The identity specializations give the unchanged auxiliary
+corners; the corank-one growth fronts use the same nonzero line coordinates.
+
+Each new local projector or nested difference is nevertheless a DIFFERENT
+matrix multiset. The profiler must enumerate the complete actual transitions
+of the new DAG and its ORIGINAL carrier assignment. It computes fixed-I+J
+matrices, not ordinary generic profiles from positive ranks. Original-envelope
+projectors retain the diagonal-mask plus rank-two formula, so differences
+have mask plus rank at most four; the inherited dimension-specific numerator
+bounds, admissible primes and complete five-prime corner-rank reconstruction
+certify the new actual profile. No largest sampled rank is silently treated
+as a rational upper bound. The geometry proof and the full profile/CRT receipts
+are separate required pieces of the composition.
+
+4. Copied centers and exact accounting
+
+For each U_i, its H-orthogonal complement in fixed-I+J coordinates has pair
+ p'_i=e_i+(3h-7)/(h-9)*1,
+ xi'_i=(h-9)/(3(h+1))*1^t-(h-9)/4*e_i^t.
+All48 complements have nonzero coordinates and pairing1. They are independent
+of the addition DAG. Their singleton profile transfers by Section3.
+
+Starting from each complete ORIGINAL fixed profile, remove exactlyh old
+identity width-h cleanup calls and addh rank-one complement calls. KEEP every
+rank-(h-1) copied transform with its actual fixed profile; do not substitute
+a generic rank expansion or subtract it a second time. Replace the entire
+local contribution, rather than adding new counts to old generic counts.
+
+Let v23=1771,v25=2300,N=v23*v25=4073300. Each axis is replicated N/v_h times:
+2300 copies of23 and1771 copies of25. Set B_h=(N/v_h)R_h. Here
+ B23=84375500, B25=85856309, W=2N+B23+B25=178378409,
+ L=2300*506+1771*600=2226400.
+The copied local rank masses are hR_h+h(h-1), respectively844261 and1212575.
+Add exterior ranks B_h*(m-h), growth ranks2N*(h-1), data ranks2N*528 and
+ALL N paid rank-one endpoint corrections. The sum is
+ W*m-N+L=102565738275,
+with deficit N-L=1846900. The largest exterior child is529<575. W and total
+rank changed from PR40; only source multiplicities, geometric classes and
+center loss remain invariant. Normalized moment weights, finite bridge and
+row stock must therefore be recomputed. The separately regenerated exact
+certificate supplies the characteristic inequality,47 strict assembly
+constraints,7 margins and eventual cutoff with inherited phase inputs pinned.
+
+Boundary. This written construction and source-bound finite certificates do
+not discharge all inherited routing, ordered-affine, physical compiler,
+semantic/complex and all-size analytic assumptions. They establish this
+specific finite composition, with attribution and exact costs; no global
+optimality or unconditional multiplication theorem is claimed.
