+PR41 changed-DAG transfer audit, 2026-10-08
+
+Bounded conclusion: PASS for the finite producer/physical matching and
+original-envelope fixed-basis transfer described below. This is not an
+independent proof of all inherited analytic, routing and all-size interfaces.
+
+Pinned inputs
+PR41 d9c96297d455053b795ee58ba108d5cf892e1c04 and RaD checkpoint
+7e488e6b25dc1713c1f41baaf1cefbf677507cf3. The pinned/manifest.json records
+retrieved source/archive URLs and SHA256. Credit RaD/hipotures for changed
+association and alternating pair-order DAGs, icekylinx for the original
+producer/frame/matching and copied centers, James Chang for reversed tensor
+geometry, and all previously credited upstream contributors.
+
+Exact alternating configurations
+h23: threshold2, grouping pairs, tree support-right, mode2, seed2959617.
+h25: threshold2, grouping pairs, tree left, mode2, seed2959617.
+Both use point_policy alternating-reverse: reverse the ORDER of complete
+global pairs only for odd common points; preserve within-pair order and tail.
+The public PR41 producer_search.py alone omits this wrapper. Reproduction
+must include the pinned point_order_search.py, not merely its configuration.
+
+Fresh alternate DAG hashes are exactly
+23 af72d798492dece65efa8b40355a2f21b54398b7e2d72d20dcb48033e3686a06
+25 07e31421d13e33be3aa885a975b9a30bcb9bc866ad69c9ad080d940326875166.
+Fresh positive-label hashes also equal the archived selected-link records.
+Regeneration matches the original-envelope count/histogram fixtures exactly.
+
+Finite checks performed
+The PR41 independent compiler was rerun on BOTH complete pinned alternating
+witnesses: exact scalar JLV identity; rational signed-frame inclusion; literal
+physical role allocation; every protected output; forward rank transitions;
+reverse-complement frame incidence; copied-center histogram and rank sum.
+It passes at roles36685/48479. The association witnesses independently pass
+the same checks at CURRENT roles37620/49644. The older common-basis prose's
+37643/49755 counts are stale and were not used.
+
+Separately, original_label_audit.py imports no producer or labeler. From the
+raw DAG it reconstructs every integer support as an exact bitset, checks every
+sum disjoint, checks actual common-core and support-union propagation, checks
+every designated exclusion and total support, and verifies the full JLV
+identity. At both alternating dimensions all additions have original cores
+of size1 or2, and sources are exactly the fixed lexicographic triple lines.
+The h centers have core{i}, full support cover, and NO ordinary consumers.
+Thus the original envelopes and Ui terminal labels satisfy exactly the old
+nondegenerate envelope geometry, without using signed positive enlargement.
+
+Our independent weighted-matching/schedule_audit.py also reconstructs the
+ORIGINAL event-slot matchings on both alternate DAGs, using 5749/7565 links.
+It verifies every legal shared-operand continuation, strict event order and
+envelope inclusion; actual carrier allocation without aliasing; exact source
+coefficients at every output; all h protected copied-center terminals; and
+an arbitrary-word dirty-wrapper regression. The role counts are36685/48479,
+and copied rank savings506/600. Neither matching enters an output use.
+Its general path argument is weighted-matching/schedule-proof.txt. This is a
+separate original-envelope proof and receipt, not an inference from the
+positive-frame histogram or from the final arithmetic certificate.
+
+Complete dirty-basis controls at h8 use the SAME alternating point rule and
+both selected tree rules. Every input, target and auxiliary basis vector is
+checked in both forward and reverse-complement orientations: support-right
+has656 roles, left has648 roles. Full h23/h25 arbitrary-dirty validity follows
+from the written reversible linear wrapper, not extrapolation from h8:
+L,J,L^-1,V,L,J,L^-1,V injects JLz+JL(z+Vx)=JLVx and restores every z. The full
+finite scalar identity and physical allocation are separately checked above.
+
+Transfer to fixed I+J profiles and copied centers
+The new original projectors still have the form diagonal outside-core mask
+plus a rank-at-most-two correction, with exactly the same h23/h25 denominator
+and entry bounds. Any nested transition therefore has a 0/1 diagonal mask
+plus rank-at-most-four correction. The prior actual-denominator CRT argument
+applies to new legal pairs, but their complete actual profiles must be freshly
+computed; no old rank histogram or generic profile may substitute for them.
+
+Source triple projectors, selected fixed bases, tensor prescriptions, source
+coordinate nonvanishing, source-pair data corners, auxiliary contractions,
+and full Ui terminal labels are unchanged. The already proved restrictions
+diag(p)*A*diag(xi) transfer ANY local matrix A, so a changed ordinary envelope
+requires its actual local ordered profile, not a new tensor basis choice.
+All h copied centers still have a distinct read-only terminal use with no
+later consumer. PR36's paid copied transform and complementary cleanup apply
+to arbitrary incoming role state in both orientations. Retain the h paid
+rank-(h-1) transforms and replace only h identity cleanups by h rank-one
+complements. Paid final corrections and all data/auxiliary calls remain.
+
+Positive signed-component labels are a separate possible construction.
+Their projectors are NOT silently covered by the original-envelope rank-four
+formula. Although role counts happen to coincide in these selected records,
+the fixed-profile composition must pin the original matching and original
+transition matrices. The new complete characteristic, semantic constants,
+row stock,47 inequalities and7 margins require separate fresh arithmetic.
+
+Reproduction scope and portable publication adapter
+The initial exploration receipts above were generated under the mounted SSD
+while the source checkout and already published trees were read-only. This
